package server

const mcpDiagramExportPolicy = "Editable diagram exchange uses POST /exports/diagrams with {diagramId,format:drawio,scope?:complete|selected,nodeIds?}; it returns a 201 background job, not the file. Read only permits this exact POST plus GET status/results and exact DELETE /exports/diagrams/{jobId} cancellation. GET /exports/capabilities preserves all SVG fields and adds diagrams with drawio validation metadata, separate limits and binary result units. Selected requires unique existing node UUIDs (1..20000), exports those logical nodes and their internal connections, and rejects nodeIds in complete scope. Complete exports all stored logical nodes, including nodes hidden in temporary views; review warnings. GET /exports/diagrams/{jobId} returns real state/progress/phases and warnings. After succeeded, GET /exports/diagrams/{jobId}/result?offset=0&limit=786432 returns {jobId,format,mimeType,encoding:base64,offset,nextOffset,totalBytes,data,complete,warnings}. Offsets/limit are raw bytes. Decode every standard padded base64 data chunk independently, concatenate decoded bytes in order and follow nextOffset until complete; concatenating base64 strings can corrupt files. Save as .drawio. Cancellation accepts {} or omitted data, returns 200 cancelled, then removes the job/result. Two active jobs, four retained jobs/128 MiB, 15 minutes from creation, 120-second deadline; 100,000 source nodes/500,000 source edges, 20,000 scoped nodes/100,000 internal edges, 5,000,000 text characters, 64 MiB output and 16,777,216 coordinate/dimension units. Jobs are transient browser RAM retaining the original vault session and MCP grant; lock/reload/stop/cache clear/explicit grant changes erase them. The saved canonical 2D layout, native shapes/text/connectors, owner/status labels and simple process assumptions are editable drawing content. Editable draw.io drawings deliberately use a light drawing surface regardless of app Appearance: white base fills, dark text/connection labels/base borders, and preserved stored node/connection/mind-map color accents. Native JSON preserves full stored styling; workspace backups also retain portable appearance settings. SVG appearance is unchanged and no additional API argument is needed. Raw datasets, source files, arbitrary metadata, live capacity copies and simulation execution/results are excluded. This is not a full native backup and does not reproduce simulation behavior or 3D camera views. Native JSON/workspace backup remains the faithful model transfer."
